<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-4">4 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Chinese and North Korean forces capture Seoul</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> troops abandoned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seoul">Seoul</a> as Chinese and North Korean armies advanced, the third time the city had changed hands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korean-war">Korean War</a>. UN forces retook it in March.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-29">29 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Julius and Ethel Rosenberg convicted of espionage</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> jury found the couple guilty of conspiring to pass atomic secrets to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>. Their execution in 1953 remained controversial, especially over Ethel's role.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/anzus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anzus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/anzus">ANZUS</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">ANZUS is the security treaty signed by Australia, New Zealand and the United States in San Francisco on 1 September 1951, each pledging to act against a common danger in the Pacific.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-san-francisco" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-san-francisco.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-san-francisco">Treaty of San Francisco</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of San Francisco was signed on 8 September 1951 by Japan and 48 Allied nations, formally ending the state of war of the Second World War.</p></div></li></ol></section>
